WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.312 --> 00:00:03.312
(light piano music)

00:00:06.476 --> 00:00:10.950
- [Voiceover] Aleppo Citadel,
the Ancient City of Palmyra,

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:13.700
and the Norias of Hama;

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:16.125
all ancient heritage sites

00:00:16.125 --> 00:00:19.125
and all destroyed in the Syrian War.

00:00:22.083 --> 00:00:26.124
It's a loss, not only to
Syrians but to the entire world,

00:00:26.124 --> 00:00:29.360
and these refugee artists
are finding their own way

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.860
to rebuild what has been lost.

00:00:49.592 --> 00:00:51.673
- [Voiceover] They have been
using found materials such as:

00:00:51.673 --> 00:00:53.922
wood, clay, and even kebab skewers

00:00:53.922 --> 00:00:58.089
to make scale models of
these historical landmarks.

00:01:06.346 --> 00:01:09.037
- [Voiceover] Their work is a
way to preserve Syrian history

00:01:09.037 --> 00:01:12.454
and educate the world about the conflict.

00:02:00.697 --> 00:02:01.530
- [Voiceover] The artists say

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:04.514
that by making this work
they are drawing attention

00:02:04.514 --> 00:02:08.514
and giving what they can
to the people of Syria.

